WRT problem, I'm assuming you've saved the game and now can't
remember the randomly selected character name you chose in order to
reload the save file to carry on playing? If so, and assuming you're
using WindowsXP (people who don't specify usually are), look in
C:\Program Files\NetHack (or wherever folder you installed Nethack
to) using windows explorer. If you've got any saved games, you should
see one or more files with names of the form:

<User>-<CharacterName>.Nethack-saved-game

where <User>        = your system account name
<CharacterName> = the name of the character, which is what you want.

E.g. I've got one at the moment, "paul-Jo.Nethack-saved-game"
where Jo is the character name. Of course if you have more than one
saved game you'll have to try loading up each character name you see
there until you find the right one!

On other operating systems the nethack folder location and save file
name format will be different, so you'll have to specify which system
you use to get the right answer. OTOH, apologies if I've misunderstood
your problem and told you something that's already blindingly obvious!

